'' A variable whose type is const through a FORWARD typedef is still const (fbc error
'' 119). The typedef is resolved when 't' is first named (ChaseTypedef_), so 'i = 0' is
'' refused where 'j = 0' is, rather than lowered and caught by the post-Check pass. A
'' pointer to the aliased type stays writable. Matches fbc on lines 14 and 15.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/const-via-forward-typedef.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/const-via-forward-typedef.out
